#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If an area is contained by a rational straight line and a sixth apotome, then the side of the area is a straight line which produces with a medial area a medial whole.
----
proof:

Let the area {AB} be contained by the rational straight line {AC} and the sixth apotome {AD}.

I say that the side of the area {AB} is a straight line which produces with a medial area a medial whole.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="410" height="190" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.96 diagram" src="propX96.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the area AB (ACBD) on the rational AC and the sixth
    // apotome AD, the annex DG bisected at E, F from the application to AG,
    // the parallel EH, the rectangles DFIB and FK (IFGK), and the squares LM
    // (RMPL) and NO (PNQO) about the diameter PR, with the gnomon arc UVW.
    // Added, all hidden at rest: a solid initiallyHidden DG so the annex
    // strokes out from D; transparent segment targets (;0;0;0) AC, AD, AG,
    // EG, AF, FG, LP, PN, LN; faceless twins (;0;0;0;0) AB, AK, DK, AI, LM,
    // NO, since a lit RMPL would be raised over NO and a lit PNQO over the
    // diameter and the gnomon (#140); faceless LPOSh (L,P,O,S) and PMTNh
    // (P,M,T,N), the two rectangles LP by PN. "About the same angle" names
    // no angle, so no marker.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, D (line sliders), C (line
    // slider on the perpendicular) — the givens — G and R (line sliders) and
    // the offscreen frees. G arrives with the annex and R with the square
    // LM, so both are deferred. E, F, H, I, K, B, M, P, L, N, O, Q, S, T,
    // U, V, W are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","C","B","D","ACBD","AB","AC","AD"];
    var ANNEX = GIVEN.concat(["G","DG","AG"]);
    var BIS   = ANNEX.concat(["E","EG"]);
    var APPL  = BIS.concat(["F","AF","FG"]);
    var PAR   = APPL.concat(["H","I","K","EH","DFIB","IFGK","AK","DK","AI"]);
    var SQ1   = PAR.concat(["R","M","P","L","RMPL","LM","LP"]);
    var SQ2   = SQ1.concat(["N","O","Q","PNQO","NO","PN"]);
    var ALL   = SQ2.concat(["RP","S","T","SQ","TQ","U","V","W","UVW",
                            "LN","LPOSh","PMTNh"]);
